00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.690
He did such a good job of writing these Jim Dwight pranks.
他在编写这些吉姆捉弄德怀特的恶作剧方面做得太出色了。

295
00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:26.970
Oh, he's so smart, Jenna.
哦，他太聪明了，珍娜。

296
00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:27.950
He's so smart.
他太聪明了。

297
00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:28.370
I know.
我知道。

298
00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:29.110
He's smarty.
他真是个聪明人。

299
00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:29.610
Yeah.
是啊。

300
00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:30.070
All right.
好吧。

301
00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:33.570
So then we move into the episode and Michael is at his desk.
接着我们进入这一集，迈克尔坐在他的办公桌前。

302
00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:34.730
Jan enters.
简进来了。

303
00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.270
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

304
00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.430
Again, like three hellos.
又是那种，连说了三声你好。

305
00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:40.910
Just call me Levinson in the morning.
早上直接叫我莱文森就行。

306
00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:43.270
In the morning, Levinson's.
早上好，莱文森。

307
00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.730
And, you know, Jan has news to deliver.
然后，你知道，简有消息要宣布。

308
00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:51.350
But first she has to sit through this barrage of awkward hellos from Michael.
但她得先忍受迈克尔那一连串尴尬的问候。

309
00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:56.110
And she finally tells him, Dunder Mifflin Scranton is closing.
最后她告诉他，邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司要关门了。

310
00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:58.770
You are a severance package person.
你属于那种拿遣散费的人。

311
00:14:58.770 --> 00:14:59.050
Yeah.
是啊。

312
00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:00.450
You're not going to make it.
你没戏了。

313
00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:01.250
Michael starts crying.
迈克尔开始哭了起来。

314
00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.890
And then he starts like moaning.
然后他开始发出那种呻吟声。

315
00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:04.850
Like how awkward.
太尴尬了。

316
00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.950
Jenna, can you imagine like in this moment?
珍娜，你能想象当时的情景吗？

317
00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:09.050
No.
不能。

318
00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:10.510
And of course, it's so loud.
而且当然，声音特别大。

319
00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:16.330
Everyone from outside the office can see and hear that something is going down in his office.
办公室外面的每个人都能看到并听到他办公室里出事了。

320
00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:17.650
Everyone's very curious.
大家都很好奇。

321
00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:22.030
Yes, because he's like, like he's moaning.
没错，因为他当时在，在呻吟。

322
00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:26.070
Kevin comes over to Pam's desk, wants to know what's going on.
凯文走到帕姆的桌前，想知道发生了什么。

323
00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.190
We had a fan question.
我们有个粉丝提问。

324
00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.610
Okay, I'm going to let this fan question go.
好吧，这个粉丝提问我就先放一放。

325
00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:35.710
And then I have a card that just says, what?
然后我这儿有张卡片上只写着，什么？

326
00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:38.990
Is it what Hadley Horton is wondering?
是哈德利·霍顿想问的那个吗？

327
00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:41.190
Why is Pam's hair different?
为什么帕姆的发型变了？

328
00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.730
What's up with the low pony?
那个低马尾是怎么回事？

329
00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:47.030
Oh, that's a separate card called low pony, question mark.
哦，那是另一张卡片，上面写着低马尾，问号。

330
00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:47.830
Okay.
好的。

331
00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.470
Where should we start?
我们从哪儿开始？

332
00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.070
Should we start with what or low pony?
是从什么开始，还是从低马尾开始？

333
00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.890
Let's start with what and then go into low pony.
我们先从什么开始，然后再聊低马尾。

334
00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:55.670
Great.
太棒了。

335
00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:01.490
Pam calls Kevin Kev and then Buddy and they fist bump.
帕姆叫凯文凯夫，然后叫他伙计，接着他们碰了下拳。

336
00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.610
What is happening?
发生了什么？

337
00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.270
What is happening?
到底发生了什么？

338
00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.470
The fist bump was a reluctant fist bump though, Ange.
安吉，那个碰拳可是很不情愿的碰拳。

339
00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.830
I know, but Kev, Buddy, fist bump.
我知道，但凯夫、伙计、碰拳。

340
00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:10.330
She's being condescending.
她在表现得居高临下。

341
00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.310
She's being totally condescending.
她表现得完全是居高临下。

342
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.710
She's trying to put him off.
她想打发走他。

343
00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:17.950
She's like, Kev, Buddy, fist bump, leave my desk.
她就像是，凯夫，伙计，碰拳，离开我的桌子。

344
00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.610
I mean, she's trying to get through it.
我是说，她只是想应付过去。

345
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:21.930
That's my interpretation.
这是我的解读。

346
00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:25.850
My interpretation was that he's like a little kid.
我的解读是她把他当成小孩子看。

347
00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:26.610
Yeah.
是啊。

348
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.250
Yeah.
是啊。

349
00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.430
So she's like, okay, Kev.
所以她就像是，好吧，凯夫。

350
00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.630
She's patronizing him for sure.
她绝对是在对他摆出那种屈尊俯就的态度。

351
00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:37.170
But you just don't often hear Pam sort of become that casual with Kevin.
但你很少听到帕姆对凯文表现得那么随意。

352
00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:41.070
Or, you know, I feel like she saves that part of herself for Jim and everyone else.
或者说，我觉得她把那一面留给了吉姆和其他人。

353
00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:44.290
She's sort of just aloof to a little bit.
她对凯文多少有点冷淡。

354
00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.510
So it just kind of was startling to me.
所以这让我感到有点惊讶。

355
00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.870
That and your low ponytail.
还有你那个低马尾。

356
00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.190
I mean, what the heck?
我是说，搞什么鬼？

357
00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.630
Here's the deal with the low pony.
关于那个低马尾，情况是这样的。

358
00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.790
I think it was a swing and a miss.
我觉得那次尝试失败了。

359
00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.730
I wasn't crazy about it when I saw it.
我当时看到的时候就不太喜欢。

360
00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:00.690
But we were trying to change things up.
但我们当时想做出一些改变。

361
00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:07.830
You might notice as well, Pam has got a little bit of like a pinkier, sparklier eyeshadow on in this episode as well.
你可能也注意到了，帕姆在这一集里还画了稍微偏粉色、带点闪光的眼影。

362
00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:08.870
And a little lip gloss.
还涂了一点唇彩。

363
00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:09.810
There's so much pink.
粉色太多了。

364
00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.910
She has pink eyeshadow, pink lipstick, pink sweater.
她有粉色眼影、粉色口红、粉色毛衣。

365
00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:16.150
But then the low pony with the clip.
然后又是那个带发夹的低马尾。

366
00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.110
Not even a ponytail holder.
甚至连发圈都不是。

367
00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.390
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

368
00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:19.650
Wait.
等等。

369
00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:20.570
I sounded so Southern.
我刚才听起来太像南方人了。

370
00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.750
It's very hard for me.
这对我来说很难。

371
00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:22.590
Holder.
发圈。

372
00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.350
Anyway, it's a clip holding your hair, not even a ponytail holder.
总之，那是个夹头发的发夹，根本不是发圈。

373
00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.610
Yeah, well, the clip is humongous.
是啊，那个发夹大得离谱。

374
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:30.990
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

375
00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:41.710
The conversation in hair and makeup was that Pam would be experimenting a little bit because she's going to her art classes.
当时在化妆间讨论的结果是，帕姆应该尝试一些新造型，因为她要去上艺术课了。

376
00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.450
She's living on her own.
她开始独立生活了。

377
00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:54.830
We needed to see some physical representation of the fact that she's attempting, even in small ways, to break out of her shell right now, to break out of her routines.
我们需要通过外在表现来体现她正在尝试突破自我，哪怕只是小小的尝试，她想打破常规。

378
00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.230
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

379
00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.010
We offer the low pony.
我们推出了低马尾造型。

380
00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:05.870
I'm going to say I think you never see it again because it wasn't great.
我敢说你以后再也不会看到它了，因为它确实不怎么样。

381
00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.990
Can we just say it wasn't great?
我们能直接说它不怎么样吗？

382
00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:09.430
It's a clip low pony.
那是发夹低马尾。

383
00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:10.530
Yeah.
是啊。

384
00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.430
A clip low pony.
发夹低马尾。

385
00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:14.150
Now, I kind of wish they'd really gone for it.
现在，我倒有点希望他们当时能更彻底一点。

386
00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.870
Next week, you would have had a banana clip.
下周你本可以戴个香蕉夹的。

387
00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:16.890
Remember those things?
还记得那东西吗？

388
00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:17.430
Oh, God.
天哪。

389
00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:18.890
They gave you like a mohawk.
那玩意儿会让你看起来像留了个莫霍克发型。

390
00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:20.190
Yeah.
是啊。

391
00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:20.730
Yeah.
是啊。

392
00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:21.770
All right.
好吧。

393
00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.910
Well, it was a moment in time.
总之，那是一个特定的时期。

394
00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.590
It was something we tried.
那是我们的一次尝试。

395
00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:29.850
Unfortunately, it's there for us all to see again and again.
不幸的是，它留在了那里，供我们一遍又一遍地观看。

396
00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:30.310
Okay.
好吧。

397
00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.110
Don't say unfortunately to me.
别对我用“不幸”这个词。

398
00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.530
Do you see how many low ponies my character has?
你知道我的角色有多少个低马尾造型吗？

399
00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.350
Like all the crazy hair views I have.
就像我那些疯狂的发型一样。

400
00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:38.130
Listen, I don't have a problem with a low pony.
听着，我对低马尾本身没什么意见。

401
00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.290
I don't have a problem with a low pony in general.
我个人对低马尾没什么意见。

402
00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:46.910
I'm just saying this particular low pony was, because of the giant clip, it was odd.
我只是说这个特定的低马尾，因为那个巨大的发夹，看起来很奇怪。

403
00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.790
We're back in Michael's office.
我们回到了迈克尔的办公室。

404
00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.310
And Jenna, I don't know if you've ever had to fire someone.
珍娜，我不知道你有没有解雇过别人。

405
00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.370
I have.
我有过。

406
00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.270
Or if you've ever been fired.
或者你有没有被解雇过。

407
00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.350
But I couldn't imagine getting the news Michael got.
但我无法想象迈克尔当时听到那个消息时的心情。

408
00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:06.710
And Jan's like, well, you know, they believe that Josh Porter is going to have a big role in the future of the company.
简当时说，嗯，你知道，他们认为乔什·波特在公司的未来中将扮演重要角色。

409
00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:09.090
And Michael goes, what kind of role?
迈克尔就问，什么角色？

410
00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.850
King of the king of the stupid universe.
蠢货宇宙之王。

411
00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:12.290
Yeah.
没错。

412
00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:14.130
Could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

413
00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:19.310
Like firing someone, basically, who's having this kind of a spiral?
解雇一个正处于这种崩溃状态的人？

414
00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:19.910
I mean.
我是说。

415
00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:26.150
Could you imagine firing someone or being fired and then having their wind up mechanical teeth?
你能想象解雇某人或被解雇时，对方突然拿出发条假牙吗？

416
00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:27.090
Was that in the script?
那是剧本里写的吗？

417
00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:28.330
It was an accident.
那是意外。

418
00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:39.170
And by the way, this points to what amazing actors Steve and Melora are, because they just stayed in the moment and reacted to it as if that was meant to happen.
顺便说一句，这体现了史蒂夫和梅洛拉是多么出色的演员，因为他们完全沉浸在情境中，反应得就像那是预先安排好的一样。

419
00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.650
It was not meant to happen.
那本来不是预先安排的。

420
00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:50.010
And could it be more brilliant that you're firing this guy who's so incompetent on so many levels and his clacky teeth go off?
而且，你正在解雇这个在各方面都如此无能的家伙，结果他的假牙突然响了起来，还有比这更绝的吗？

421
00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:51.810
Yes.
确实。

422
00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.190
Amazing.
太棒了。

423
00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:54.150
All right.
好了。

424
00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:55.790
I'm going to move us along.
我们要继续往下说了。

425
00:19:56.150 --> 00:20:01.630
Michael has a talking head where he says, let's see Josh find another Stanley, Phyllis, or Kevin.
迈克尔有一个单人访谈，他说，让乔什去再找一个斯坦利、菲利斯或凯文试试看。

426
00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:02.850
Show me that farm.
让我看看那个农场。

427
00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.450
Show me that farm.
让我看看那个农场。

428
00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:11.090
And during that talking head, we kind of, we see Creed eating his mung beans at his desk.
在那段访谈中，我们看到克里德在办公桌前吃绿豆。

429
00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:13.450
We see Phyllis knitting.
我们看到菲利斯在织毛衣。

430
00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.690
And we had a fan question from Stephanie Miller.
我们收到了粉丝斯蒂芬妮·米勒的一个问题。

431
00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:19.730
In this episode, when we see Phyllis knitting, can she knit in real life?
在这一集中，当我们看到菲利斯织毛衣时，她在现实生活中会织毛衣吗？

432
00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:22.430
Did she knit that whole scarf her character is working on?
她角色正在织的那条围巾是她自己织的吗？

433
00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:25.390
You guys, she is 100% fake knitting.
各位，她完全是在假装织毛衣。

434
00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:26.710
Phyllis cannot knit.
菲利斯根本不会织毛衣。

435
00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:28.490
Didn't she do so good?
她演得不是很好吗？

436
00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.470
They had a basket full of knitting stuff.
他们准备了一个装满编织用品的篮子。

437
00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:31.810
They'd made it part of her character.
他们把它变成了她角色的一部分。

438
00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:35.290
It's set next to her desk all nine seasons.
九季以来，它一直放在她的办公桌旁。

439
00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:37.030
And it just sat there.
就一直放在那儿。

440
00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.850
And sometimes if she had to do background stuff.
有时如果她需要做背景动作的话。

441
00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:45.250
But this was a great panning shot because, you know, Michael says there is no Stanley tree and he's napping.
但这真是一个很棒的平移镜头，因为迈克尔说没有斯坦利树，而他正在打瞌睡。

442
00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:49.570
And then they said, do you think the world is crawling with Phyllis's and she's knitting?
然后他们说，你觉得世界上到处都是菲利斯，而且都在织毛衣吗？

443
00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.290
So it was this great visual.
所以这是一个很棒的视觉效果。

444
00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.930
But no, Phyllis can't knit.
但不是，菲利斯不会织毛衣。

445
00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:53.670
Yeah.
是的。

446
00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:54.790
No.
不会。

447
00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:55.690
No.
不会。

448
00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:57.950
That's one of my favorite talking heads, though.
不过那是我最喜欢的单人访谈之一。

449
00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:58.790
I love that one.
我很喜欢那一段。

450
00:20:59.010 --> 00:20:59.750
I do, too.
我也是。

451
00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:00.610
I do, too.
我也是。

452
00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.670
So then Michael is walking around the office.
于是迈克尔在办公室里走来走去。

453
00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.670
Dwight can tell something's wrong, but Michael isn't spilling.
德怀特看出他不对劲，但迈克尔就是不肯说。

454
00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:17.150
And this is my other favorite talking head from this episode, which is Dwight's talking head, where he says, when you're close to someone, you can read them like a book.
这是这一集中我另一个最喜欢的采访镜头，是德怀特的采访，他说，当你和某人很亲近时，你就能像读一本书一样读懂他们。

455
00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:25.110
And he says, Michael's book is titled, Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?
他说，迈克尔这本书的书名是《有怪事发生：简说了什么？》

456
00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:30.970
The Michael Scott Story by Michael Scott with Dwight Schrute.
《迈克尔·斯科特的故事》，作者迈克尔·斯科特，德怀特·舒鲁特协助。

457
00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.730
All right, that last part is not in the script,
好吧，最后那部分剧本里没有，

458
00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:43.210
and I could kind of tell that there was an improv there because whenever Rain improvs at the end of a talking head or the end of a scene,
我能看出来那是即兴发挥，因为每当雷恩在采访或场景结束时即兴表演，

459
00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:48.810
I feel like you can see him smile just a little bit in the corners of his mouth and his eyes.
我觉得你能看到他的嘴角和眼睛里有一丝笑意。

460
00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:57.110
So I reached out to Mike Schur, and he told me that he and Rain expanded on the book title on the day, on set.
所以我联系了迈克·舒尔，他告诉我，他和雷恩是在拍摄当天在片场扩展了书名。

461
00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:58.590
They kept throwing out ideas.
他们一直在抛出各种点子。

462
00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:03.410
The original was just supposed to be Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?
原本的台词应该只是《有怪事发生：简说了什么？》

463
00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:09.050
And Mike threw out the Michael Scott story, and then Rain added with Dwight Schrute.
迈克提议加上《迈克尔·斯科特的故事》，然后雷恩又加了“德怀特·舒鲁特协助”。

464
00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:10.190
Yeah, for sure.
没错，确实如此。

465
00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.330
I mean, I feel like we all have tells.
我是说，我觉得我们都有自己的“马脚”。

466
00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:18.450
And Rain, when he has an improv that I think he's really happy with, has a little bit of a smirk.
雷恩在即兴表演时，如果他对自己很满意，嘴角就会露出一丝坏笑。

467
00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:20.210
He's kind of proud of the moment.
他对自己那一刻的表现感到有点自豪。

468
00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.690
He amuses himself in the moment while saying it.
他在说出那句话时，自己也觉得很有趣。

469
00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:32.110
Now things are really getting heightened over at the Stanford branch because Karen breaks the news that the Scranton branch is closing to Jim, and oh my God, Jim's face.
现在斯坦福分部的情况真的变得紧张起来了，因为凯伦告诉吉姆斯克兰顿分部要关闭了，天哪，吉姆的表情。

470
00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:33.030
He's like, what?
他一脸震惊，心想：什么？

471
00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.450
You notice he doesn't reach out to Pam.
你注意到他没有联系帕姆。

472
00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:39.570
Pam and Jim never call one another or text one another in this whole day.
这一整天，帕姆和吉姆都没有打电话或发短信给对方。

473
00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:47.910
It's kind of weird because in Diwali, we see that Pam was texting Jim, and they had that phone call.
这有点奇怪，因为在排灯节那集，我们看到帕姆给吉姆发了短信，他们还通了电话。

474
00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:49.670
At the end of grief counseling.
在悲伤辅导结束时。

475
00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:51.810
But what's going on?
但到底发生了什么？

476
00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:53.090
Why no communication?
为什么没有沟通？

477
00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.010
It makes perfect sense to me.
我觉得这完全说得通。

478
00:22:55.230 --> 00:22:59.910
You know, they're both sort of struggling with where do we go from here?
你知道，他们都在纠结接下来该怎么办。

479
00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:08.070
And I'm sure Pam's first instinct is to reach out to him, but she doesn't feel like she has that kind of access to him anymore.
我相信帕姆的第一直觉是联系他，但她觉得她已经没有那种权限去联系他了。

480
00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:09.530
She rejected him.
她拒绝了他。

481
00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:12.290
So, no, it makes perfect sense to me that they don't communicate.
所以，我觉得他们不沟通完全合情合理。

482
00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:17.390
What I thought was weirder, and we're going to get to it, is that Roy finds out from accounting.
我觉得更奇怪的是——我们待会儿会讲到——罗伊是从会计部那里得知的消息。

483
00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:19.730
So Pam didn't even tell Roy.
所以帕姆甚至没告诉罗伊。

484
00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:20.650
That's right.
没错。

485
00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:24.230
So now Michael approaches Pam at front reception.
现在迈克尔走向前台接待处的帕姆。

486
00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:25.870
He's acting really strange.
他表现得非常奇怪。

487
00:23:26.110 --> 00:23:32.230
She clearly knows something is up because he was moaning in his office, and Jan visited.
她显然知道出事了，因为他刚才在办公室里呻吟，而且简来过。

488
00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:34.410
So Pam's like, what's going on, Michael?
所以帕姆问，迈克尔，怎么了？

489
00:23:35.150 --> 00:23:35.870
Yeah.
没错。

490
00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.250
I have a fan catch from this moment.
我有一个粉丝发现的细节。

491
00:23:38.530 --> 00:23:39.110
Okay.
好的。

492
00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:43.430
At 6 minutes, 21 seconds, Celeste Dimas says,
在6分21秒，塞莱斯特·迪马斯说，

493
00:23:43.670 --> 00:23:48.930
If you freeze and look closely on that big board that's hanging by accounting,
如果你暂停仔细看会计部旁边挂着的那块大板子，

494
00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:51.830
on Tuesday the 5th, it says,
在5号星期二那天，上面写着，

495
00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:56.490
One of many Emmys, Steve, was robbed.
“史蒂夫本该获得众多艾美奖之一，却被抢走了”。

496
00:23:56.490 --> 00:24:00.430
Oh, that's a great fan catch.
哦，那真是个很棒的粉丝发现。

497
00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:02.150
I promise I didn't write it.
我保证那不是我写的。

498
00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:05.330
We shot this episode about two weeks after the Emmys,
我们是在艾美奖颁奖典礼后大约两周拍摄的这一集，

499
00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:10.790
and I guess someone had written up on the board a little congratulations to us,
我想应该是有人在板子上写了点祝贺我们的话，

500
00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:15.410
and we also needed to say that Steve was robbed because he did not win that year for Michael Scott.
我们也需要写上史蒂夫被抢走了奖项，因为他那年没能凭借迈克尔·斯科特这个角色获奖。

501
00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.370
He never won for Michael Scott.
他从未凭迈克尔·斯科特这个角色获奖。

502
00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:18.990
Which is ridiculous.
这太荒谬了。

503
00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:19.690
Yeah.
是啊。

504
00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:26.730
Well, I have a Jenna catch, because since Celeste turned me on to looking at this whiteboard,
嗯，我有个发现，因为自从塞莱斯特提醒我去看这块白板后，

505
00:24:26.950 --> 00:24:28.790
I found something else on the whiteboard.
我在白板上又发现了别的东西。

506
00:24:29.110 --> 00:24:34.090
On the top line written under Thursday, written in multiple colors, it says,
在周四那一行的上方，用多种颜色写着：

507
00:24:34.250 --> 00:24:37.730
In case you haven't noticed, there is a lot of colorful hooey on this board.
如果你还没注意到的话，这块板子上有很多花里胡哨的废话。

508
00:24:39.430 --> 00:24:43.850
Anyway, guys, for the future, I think it could be very fun to freeze on this whiteboard,
总之，伙计们，以后我觉得如果能定格看看这块白板会很有趣，

509
00:24:44.010 --> 00:24:46.130
because they did change what they wrote all the time.
因为他们一直在改写上面的内容。

510
00:24:46.270 --> 00:24:47.090
Well, I love that.
嗯，我喜欢这个。

511
00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:54.150
I love the little subtle shade towards the television academy about Steve not getting the Emmy.
我喜欢这种对电视学院含蓄的讽刺，因为史蒂夫没拿到艾美奖。

512
00:24:54.970 --> 00:24:55.210
Totally.
完全同意。

513
00:24:55.570 --> 00:24:59.550
Coming up next, Michael has a talking head, and then he does something immediately after,
接下来，迈克尔有个采访镜头，紧接着他做了一件事，

514
00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:03.090
and it's one of these classic Michael moments that I live for.
那是迈克尔的经典时刻之一，我简直太爱了。

515
00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:04.650
It always makes me laugh so hard.
每次都让我笑得不行。

516
00:25:05.050 --> 00:25:10.410
Michael says that all he can do is put on a brave face and be our leader.
迈克尔说他唯一能做的就是强颜欢笑，继续做我们的领导。

517
00:25:10.650 --> 00:25:13.250
And then he says to the whole bullpen,
然后他对整个办公区的人说：

518
00:25:13.450 --> 00:25:14.390
It's over.
一切都结束了。

519
00:25:14.390 --> 00:25:15.890
We are screwed.
我们完蛋了。

520
00:25:16.270 --> 00:25:16.630
Yeah.
是啊。

521
00:25:16.630 --> 00:25:18.110
Like, really, buddy?
我说，真的吗，老兄？

522
00:25:18.290 --> 00:25:20.210
That's the brave face you're putting on for us?
这就是你给我们展示的强颜欢笑？

523
00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:21.030
Okay, thanks.
好吧，谢谢。

524
00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:24.590
Yeah, I mean, he really, he offers no comfort.
是啊，我是说，他真的，他一点安慰都没给。

525
00:25:24.590 --> 00:25:26.970
He sort of begins to ugly cry.
他开始那种丑陋的哭相了。

526
00:25:27.490 --> 00:25:31.050
Angela is asking about the employees, asking about their jobs.
安吉拉在问员工们的情况，问他们的工作。

527
00:25:31.250 --> 00:25:32.950
I have two catches here.
我这里有两个发现。

528
00:25:33.110 --> 00:25:35.150
I have something I need to say, Angela.
安吉拉，我有话要说。

529
00:25:35.430 --> 00:25:35.910
Okay, go.
好的，你说。

530
00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:39.730
At 7 minutes, 18 seconds, your sweater?
在7分18秒的时候，你的毛衣？

531
00:25:39.730 --> 00:25:40.750
It's a sweater?
那是毛衣吗？

532
00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:41.250
It's a sweater veSt.
那是件毛背心。

533
00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:47.390
Okay, so I actually have some photos of this sweater from a wardrobe fitting that I saved.
好吧，其实我保存了一些试装时拍的这件毛衣的照片。

534
00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:54.490
So I have a button-down shirt, and then over it, I have a sweater vest, but it's like a tank.
我穿了一件衬衫，外面套了件毛背心，但它像个背心裙。

535
00:25:54.490 --> 00:26:00.550
It's like a teeny, tiny, very odd sweater veSt.
那是一件极小、非常奇怪的毛背心。

536
00:26:00.810 --> 00:26:06.230
It's like another one of those failed project runway contests.
就像是《决战时装伸展台》里又一个失败的作品。

537
00:26:06.230 --> 00:26:07.690
Oh, 100%.
噢，百分之百是。

538
00:26:07.690 --> 00:26:16.230
And then our wardrobe designer, Carrie Bennett, took the buttons off the sweater vest and replaced them with those cat faces.
然后我们的服装设计师凯莉·贝内特把毛背心上的扣子拆掉，换成了那些猫脸扣子。

539
00:26:16.530 --> 00:26:17.870
It's really a work of art.
这真是一件艺术品。

540
00:26:18.150 --> 00:26:19.010
It really is.
确实是。

541
00:26:19.010 --> 00:26:20.570
All right, well, I have a catch.
好吧，我也有个发现。

542
00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:26.490
At 7 minutes, 27 seconds, this is one of the most famous Michael Scott memes.
在7分27秒的时候，这是迈克尔·斯科特最著名的表情包之一。

543
00:26:26.830 --> 00:26:33.030
It's Steve making that face, like he's about to cry, or maybe he smells dog poop.
就是史蒂夫做出的那个表情，好像快要哭出来，或者闻到了狗屎味。

544
00:26:33.190 --> 00:26:33.650
You know the face.
你知道那个表情。

545
00:26:33.710 --> 00:26:35.970
And he says, this is the worSt.
他说：这是最糟糕的。

546
00:26:36.010 --> 00:26:41.810
And people use it a ton to respond to other people, like when they get some news that they're like, no way.
人们经常用它来回复别人，比如当他们收到什么消息觉得“不会吧”的时候。

547
00:26:41.810 --> 00:26:45.730
All of a sudden, I see in my feed Steve's face.
我突然就在我的动态里看到了史蒂夫的脸。

548
00:26:45.730 --> 00:26:51.970
Okay, on Office Ladies Pod, will you please post the pictures of your cat buttons and of this meme?
好的，在《办公室女士》播客上，你能发布一下你的猫脸扣子照片和这个表情包吗？

549
00:26:52.450 --> 00:26:54.230
Yes, of course, of course.
当然，当然可以。

550
00:26:54.390 --> 00:26:56.890
Okay, good, because I want everyone to have these visuals.
太好了，因为我想让每个人都能看到这些画面。

551
00:26:57.650 --> 00:26:59.250
Okay, I think it's important.
好吧，我觉得这很重要。

552
00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:03.010
I have a script question, Jenna, because I know you have the scripts.
Jenna，我有个关于剧本的问题，因为我知道剧本在你那儿。

553
00:27:04.790 --> 00:27:08.050
So, Toby admits that he knows that this was going to happen.
Toby承认他知道这件事会发生。

554
00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:10.750
Michael calls him a traitor, says he wants to see him in his office.
Michael骂他是叛徒，说要让他去办公室见他。

555
00:27:11.190 --> 00:27:15.610
They start to walk in, and Michael says, oh, my God, you walk so slowly.
他们开始往里走，Michael说，天哪，你走得太慢了。

556
00:27:15.730 --> 00:27:17.530
I feel like that was Steve improvising.
我觉得那是Steve即兴发挥的。

557
00:27:17.730 --> 00:27:20.310
I had that same feeling, and I did look at the script.
我也有同感，我查了剧本。

558
00:27:20.690 --> 00:27:25.150
None of that part of him calling Toby into his office was scripted.
他叫Toby去办公室那一段根本没写在剧本里。

559
00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:31.030
So, him, that whole bit of him calling Toby in his office, say he's walking slowly,
所以，他叫Toby去办公室，说他走得慢的那整段戏，

560
00:27:31.250 --> 00:27:36.110
and then Dwight guarding the door and putting his hand up to the camera, none of that was in the script.
还有Dwight守在门口把手挡在镜头前，这些剧本里都没有。

561
00:27:36.910 --> 00:27:37.350
Amazing.
太棒了。

562
00:27:37.970 --> 00:27:38.250
Yeah.
是啊。

563
00:27:38.410 --> 00:27:38.710
Amazing.
太棒了。

564
00:27:38.970 --> 00:27:40.490
And I love that everyone just went with it.
我喜欢大家顺着他演的样子。

565
00:27:40.650 --> 00:27:42.830
They just were like, oh, Steve's doing his thing.
他们就像是，哦，Steve又在搞他的那一套了。

566
00:27:42.990 --> 00:27:45.030
We're going to let this play out and participate.
我们要让这出戏演下去，并参与其中。

567
00:27:45.730 --> 00:27:50.170
Because I looked, I was like, wait, is there a lost scene of Toby in Michael's office?
因为我查了，我当时想，等等，是不是有一段Toby在Michael办公室的戏被删了？

568
00:27:50.350 --> 00:27:52.630
Is there a conversation that didn't make it?
是不是有一段对话没放进去？

569
00:27:52.790 --> 00:27:53.130
No.
没有。

570
00:27:53.370 --> 00:27:56.030
No, that was just Steve on the day.
没有，那纯粹是Steve当天的即兴发挥。

571
00:27:56.390 --> 00:27:56.630
Wow.
哇。

572
00:27:56.830 --> 00:28:01.150
And, you know, speaking of how Rain gets the little smirk when he improvises,
说到Rain即兴表演时会露出那种小窃笑，

573
00:28:01.470 --> 00:28:08.810
at 7 minutes 52 seconds, when he won't let the camera crew in and he shuts the door, he has the smirk.
在7分52秒，当他不让摄制组进去并关上门时，他露出了那种窃笑。

574
00:28:08.970 --> 00:28:10.070
I noticed it, too.
我也注意到了。

575
00:28:11.370 --> 00:28:17.010
Well, we had a fan question from Mary Poulton, and actually a lot of people wrote in with a similar question.
嗯，我们收到一个来自Mary Poulton的粉丝提问，其实很多人都问过类似的问题。

576
00:28:17.910 --> 00:28:26.330
She wanted to know, when we got the script for this episode, did any of us worry that the show was being canceled?
她想知道，当我们拿到这一集的剧本时，有没有人担心剧集要被砍了？

577
00:28:26.530 --> 00:28:29.710
Or did we know that this was just an idea for an episode?
还是说我们知道这只是剧情的一个点？

578
00:28:30.590 --> 00:28:38.130
And she was asking, and a lot of people were asking, because we've said before, sometimes plots are revealed to us at these table reads, and they were shocking.
她这么问，很多人也这么问，因为我们之前说过，有时剧情是在剧本围读会上才揭晓的，而且非常令人震惊。

579
00:28:38.410 --> 00:28:44.210
And they wanted to know, as we sat down and got the script, as we were reading it, were we thinking, wait a second, what?
他们想知道，当我们坐下来拿到剧本，在读的时候，有没有想过，等等，什么情况？

580
00:28:44.390 --> 00:28:46.030
Scranton's closing, are we all out of jobs?
Scranton分部要关了，我们都要失业了吗？

581
00:28:46.510 --> 00:28:49.170
No, guys, we knew that this was a plot point.
不，伙计们，我们知道这只是一个剧情点。

582
00:28:49.810 --> 00:28:51.610
None of us were worried.
我们没人担心。

583
00:28:51.610 --> 00:28:55.330
We had all had our contracts renewed for all of season three.
我们所有人的第三季合同都已经续签了。

584
00:28:55.630 --> 00:28:55.910
Yeah.
没错。

585
00:28:56.490 --> 00:29:00.530
And so we knew that we would be producing 24 episodes in season three.
所以我们知道第三季会制作24集。

586
00:29:00.710 --> 00:29:08.290
And we also had been tipped off to the fact that eventually there would be a merger episode, and that those people from Stanford would be coming to join us.
而且我们也提前得知最终会有一集合并的戏，Stanford的人会加入我们。

587
00:29:08.410 --> 00:29:12.270
So we didn't have any kind of surprise or anxiety when we got this script.
所以拿到这个剧本时，我们没有任何惊讶或焦虑。

588
00:29:12.530 --> 00:29:17.990
No, we were just excited because it meant finally, after this episode, we could all be in one room together.
不，我们只是很兴奋，因为这意味着终于，在这一集之后，我们大家都能聚在一个房间里了。

589
00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:19.310
So we were excited.
所以我们很兴奋。

590
00:29:19.450 --> 00:29:21.430
At least the Scranton branch, we were excited.
至少Scranton分部的人很兴奋。

591
00:29:21.590 --> 00:29:21.910
I don't know.
我不知道。

592
00:29:22.130 --> 00:29:26.230
Maybe Stanford was like, we like our schedule, but we were excited to have everyone back.
也许Stanford的人会想，我们喜欢现在的安排，但我们很高兴能让大家团聚。

593
00:29:26.530 --> 00:29:27.010
All right.
好的。

594
00:29:27.110 --> 00:29:32.970
So now, Angela, we move into Orion talking head, and he's holding up his business cards, right?
那么现在，Angela，我们进入Orion的个人访谈，他举着他的名片，对吧？

595
00:29:33.050 --> 00:29:34.870
Or are they his calling cards?
还是说那是他的拜访卡？

596
00:29:35.370 --> 00:29:36.190
Oh, boy.
天哪。

597
00:29:36.310 --> 00:29:36.750
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

598
00:29:37.030 --> 00:29:40.630
He's holding up his business slash calling cards.
他举着他的名片兼拜访卡。

599
00:29:40.790 --> 00:29:40.950
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

600
00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:42.430
Eight minutes.
八分钟。

601
00:29:43.070 --> 00:29:47.430
Notice, here it is, talking head, exterior window behind him.
注意看，这里是访谈镜头，他身后是外景窗。

602
00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:49.430
Oh, nice.
哦，真不错。

603
00:29:49.430 --> 00:29:58.150
This is the beginning of the exterior window talking heads, because next up, Angela has a talking head, and Kelly has a talking head, with the mascara on her face,
这是外景窗访谈镜头的开端，因为接下来安吉拉有段访谈，凯莉也有段访谈，脸上还涂着睫毛膏，

604
00:29:58.290 --> 00:29:59.690
all exterior windows.
全都是外景窗。

605
00:29:59.990 --> 00:30:01.510
She's gonna track it.
她会追踪这个细节。

606
00:30:01.690 --> 00:30:02.210
All right.
好的。

607
00:30:02.270 --> 00:30:06.390
So now we're going back to Stanford, and Andy is leading everyone in a chant.
现在我们回到斯坦福分部，安迪正带领大家喊口号。

608
00:30:06.550 --> 00:30:07.730
Stanford, Connecticut.
康涅狄格州的斯坦福。

609
00:30:09.210 --> 00:30:09.730
Right?
对吧？

610
00:30:09.890 --> 00:30:11.090
He's getting everyone worked up.
他正在调动大家的情绪。

611
00:30:11.090 --> 00:30:19.770
So while everyone's chanting, at eight minutes, 23 seconds, you will see someone who is beloved by our office cast and crew.
在大家喊口号时，在8分23秒处，你会看到一位深受我们办公室演职人员喜爱的人。

612
00:30:19.870 --> 00:30:20.890
Her name is Lori Sox.
她叫洛里·索克斯。

613
00:30:21.030 --> 00:30:22.270
She was our stand-in.
她是我们的替身演员。

614
00:30:22.670 --> 00:30:26.190
Her and her husband, Stephen, they were like a stand-in duo team.
她和她丈夫斯蒂芬，他们就像是一对替身搭档。

615
00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:28.350
And she's in the background in the scene.
她出现在那个场景的背景里。

616
00:30:28.470 --> 00:30:30.250
And it just made me so happy to see her.
看到她让我感到非常开心。

617
00:30:30.570 --> 00:30:31.690
I saw her, too.
我也看到了。

618
00:30:31.890 --> 00:30:32.710
I saw her, too.
我也看到了。

619
00:30:32.770 --> 00:30:33.510
And I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

620
00:30:33.670 --> 00:30:36.790
Well, maybe we should explain what a stand-in is, if we haven't before.
嗯，也许我们该解释一下什么是替身演员，如果之前没说过的话。

621
00:30:37.470 --> 00:30:46.370
So after you rehearse a scene with the actors, you bring in people to stand-in for the actors while the crew sets the lights and the camera angles.
在演员排练完场景后，我们会请替身演员代替他们站位，以便剧组调整灯光和摄像机角度。

622
00:30:46.530 --> 00:30:54.210
And this is an opportunity for the cast to go and get their makeup fixed or change their outfit or any number of things, rehearse their lines.
这让演员们有机会去补妆、换装或做其他事情，以及背台词。

623
00:30:54.570 --> 00:30:59.810
And then when we're ready to start rolling, the actors come back in and stand in their positions or sit at their desks.
等我们准备好开拍时，演员们再回来站到各自的位置或坐在办公桌前。

624
00:30:59.810 --> 00:31:06.110
So Lori would stand-in for all the women, and Stephen, her husband, would stand-in for the men.
洛里会为所有女性角色当替身，而她丈夫斯蒂芬则为男性角色当替身。

625
00:31:06.450 --> 00:31:10.970
But every once in a while, you'll see them pop-up in the background of scenes, and that's what happened here.
但偶尔你会看到他们出现在场景背景里，这次就是这样。

626
00:31:11.430 --> 00:31:12.370
Yeah, they're wonderful.
没错，他们太棒了。

627
00:31:12.370 --> 00:31:13.950
And we all became very close.
我们大家都变得非常亲近。

628
00:31:14.210 --> 00:31:17.230
And anyway, I was very excited to see her there.
总之，能在那里看到她我非常兴奋。

629
00:31:17.470 --> 00:31:18.210
I know.
我知道。

630
00:31:18.350 --> 00:31:19.210
They were the lovelieSt.
他们是最可爱的人。

631
00:31:19.210 --> 00:31:20.410
And they had two kids.
他们还有两个孩子。

632
00:31:20.990 --> 00:31:23.590
Lori got pregnant twice over the course of the show.
洛里在剧集拍摄期间怀孕了两次。

633
00:31:23.890 --> 00:31:28.410
Everybody who worked on our show became part of the family, and they were part of our family.
每一个参与我们剧集制作的人都成了家人，他们也是我们家庭的一部分。

634
00:31:29.810 --> 00:31:29.990
Absolutely.
绝对是。

635
00:31:30.470 --> 00:31:37.270
